line	<str>Go back to the Troll Stronghold. You may skip this and use the parrot on your way back to Eadgar in the next section if using the agility way.</str>
line	
line	<str>Run north and go down both flights of stairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the parrot on the rack north of the cells.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Tegid in Taverley south-east of the Herblore store for a dirty robe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick a thistle in one of the grass patches near Eadgar's cave entrance. It is very small and coloured the same as the grass. Zoom in close on each patch to find a green flower around the patch of grass. It can be hard to see. Note that it only spawns in one of the patches of grass at a time.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter Eadgar's cave and talk to Eadgar.</str>
line	
line	<str>Light a fire with your other log and cook the thistle on it to make a dried thistle. (You may also use one of the fires near the trolls to the west.)</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the pestle and mortar on the dried thistle and add it to a ranarr potion (unf).</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Eadgar.</str>
line	
line	<str>Retrieve your parrot from the rack in the troll stronghold.</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Talk to Eadgar.</col>
step	29	-	Quick guide step 29
line	<str>Talk to Sanfew (top floor of the Taverley herblore store) , or if you have completed Zogre Flesh Eaters).</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb to the top of Trollheim, using the agility shortcuts if you can to save time, and enter Eadgar's Cave (see map for path alternatives).</str>
line	
line	<str>If you have not yet freed Eadgar in the troll stronghold's prison, pickpocket (30+ Thieving) or kill Berry the northern sleeping troll guard and use the cell key 2 on Eadgar's cell. Check your Troll Stronghold quest log and there will be a line that will either say "I've rescued Godric" or "I've rescued Godric and Mad Eadgar" to make sure.</str>
line	
line	<str>Speak with Eadgar in his cave.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go to Burntmeat's Kitchen, which is at the south end of the middle floor of the stronghold.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Burntmeat.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to Eadgar and speak with him.</str>
line	
line	<str>For the secret door path, Slayer ring teleport to the Fremennik Slayer Dungeon or use the Fairy ring with (code AJR) to teleport outside the Dungeon entrance.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head north-east to a narrow passage, climb over the rocks, and go through the secret entrance to the north.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to Burntmeat's Kitchen, which is at the south end of the middle floor of the stronghold.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Burntmeat.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go speak with Eadgar, whose cave is at the top of Trollheim.</str>
line	
line	<str>Travel to Ardougne Zoo, talk to Parroty Pete and ask him both questions.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use vodka (right click it to avoid accidentally drinking it) on the pineapple chunks.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use alco-chunks on the aviary hatch (west side of parrot cage).</str>
line	
line	<str>Do not drop the parrot or it will fly away and you will need to retrieve it from Eadgar.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Eadgar in his cave at Trollheim about making the fake human.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go back to the Troll Stronghold. You may skip this and use the parrot on your way back to Eadgar in the next section if using the agility way.</str>
